mipi_dbi: no reset on a conditional power-on of a write-only controller. It
cannot report its power mode, so the bootloader may have left it on, showing
an image. A reset turns the display off until the init sequence ends; without
one, the controller keeps showing its frame memory while the driver
reinitialises it.

--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_mipi_dbi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/drm_mipi_dbi.c
@@ -778,6 +778,10 @@
 	if (cond && mipi_dbi_display_is_on(dbi))
 		return 1;
 
+	/* Possibly on: a reset would turn the display off until reinitialised. */
+	if (cond && !dbi->read_commands)
+		return 0;
+
 	mipi_dbi_hw_reset(dbi);
 	ret = mipi_dbi_command(dbi, MIPI_DCS_SOFT_RESET);
 	if (ret) {
